{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ורמה", :translit "verimah", :gloss "and the maggot"} {:he "ורמה תכסה עליהם", :translit "verimah techaseh aleihem", :gloss "and the maggot shall cover them"} {:he "בהמוכר את הספינה", :translit "behamokher et ha-sefinah", :gloss "in [the chapter] One Who Sells the Ship"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ורמה" "ורמה תכסה עליהם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Rare word ורמה links two contexts in which decay is suspended: Shabbat and manna-eaters."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud in Bava Batra discusses the manna and states that those who ate the manna were protected from maggots and decay. The chapter is titled 'One Who Sells the Ship' (המוכר את הספינה). Separately, Shabbat 30a-b records that worms and maggots do not have dominion over a corpse on Shabbat. Ba'al HaTurim reads the two occurrences of ורמה as encoding both teachings: decay has no power over the dead on Shabbat, and maggots had no power over those who ate the manna.", :sources ["Bava Batra 17a" "Shabbat 30a" "Shabbat 30b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ורמה" "ורמה תכסה עליהם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ורמה", :refs ["Exodus 16:24" "Jeremiah 4:29" "Job 21:26"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ורמה תכסה עליהם", :refs ["Job 21:26"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Rare word ורמה links two contexts in which decay is suspended: Shabbat and manna-eaters.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:16:40.698970509Z", :model "glm-5.2"}